Z||000003||theogre||05-12-2000||10:08 AM||||check the PIM and pickup coil for the 42. If the PIM has loose wires, isn't mounted right, or bad you can get 42's.<P>check for vacuum leaks for the 44. You could have a hose coming loose when hot. (PCV and brake booster lines should be clamped at all joints. Clamp PCV elbows gently, the rubber is soft. You'll cut right thru it if you over tighten.) V6 also check complete EGR system.||||reg||1
Z||000004||chris6878||05-12-2000||09:10 PM||||thanks for the reply man...   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">   Its a v6<P>My car is getting worse...  it stumbles upon acceleration now... and wants to quit when coming to a stop....          just replaced the dis cap and rotor button today.. and it has new wires and plugs...  I dunno about this car.. .ahhh..      ||||reg||14
Z||000005||Fiasco||05-13-2000||01:53 AM||||Not sure about the codes, but you mentioned the EGR tube... if it's cracked or leaking, start there. That can definitely make it run mysteriously.||||reg||1
Z||000006||LarryB||05-14-2000||03:32 AM||||This is one of those times when a Helms manual is worth having, it has flow charts of procedures to follow, most of which you can do either by physical inspection, a test light, or an ohmmeter. <P>The code 44 (lean exhaust) can apparently be caused by any of: lean injectors, low fuel pressure, water in fuel, EGR not opening when engine is warm, O2 sensor, O2 sensor pigtail grounding, bad MAP sensor, or exhaust leak. For code 42 (spark timing) check the cabling to the ECM and to the ignition module, could also be a bad ignition module or failed ECM.<P>So, I guess the first things I'd check would be the cabling that plugs into the ECM, into the ignition module, and to the O2 sensor, look for cracks or leaks in the exhaust upstream of the O2 sensor, then check that everything else in the list above is OK. <P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by chris6878:<BR><B>also add code 42...   just checked ecm again after a 25 minute drive...    two codes this time  42, and the 44 from yesterday...     my car also takes a while for the rpm's to drop when ya rev it now, you can rev it up to 2000 rpms and it will take about 5-6 second before it drops back to 1000 rpms...  like you havent let off the gas yet...  <P>what could be the prob.. ?  egr? tube?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
