Z||000015||rogergarrison||05-17-2000||12:11 PM||||[QUOTE]Originally posted by chris6878:<BR>[B]<BR>my 2.8 started idleing very eraticly, stumbled on initial take off and when shifting gears, replacing throttle pos sensor and MAP sensor cured it. note/ be sure the MAP sensor you buy has the right color inside the wire connector. NAPA and all the GM dealers all have a replacement number for part-BUT IT WONT WORK. mine just happened to be orange and the only one listed is black. It ran like total crap. I found the correct one at AUTOZONE- now runs perfect ||||reg||1
